The four items in `.com.misc` each got their own branch. Two are finished. Two are not, and the reason is named.

1. Findings, live config. Branch `findings-live-config`, commit `ceba690d`, pushed 2026-11-02 04:26 UTC. A bad `smtp_port` written while running is named in the log and the running value is left alone. A boolean written for `poll_interval_sec` reads as 20 and the log names it, instead of becoming 1. A policy field `alllowed_kinds` is named and is not in the built policy. The tests are `runner/tests/test_live_findings.py`, four of them, all passing here.

2. Shotgun families, bugs 2 to 54. Not started. `.com.misc` and the 8:12pm forum entry name the range and say item 1, the retained-load bug, is done. Neither names bugs 2 through 54, and no numbered queue of those bugs is in the tree. No branch, and no invented families.

3. FreeBSD shell check. Not recorded. The guest phase is the run at https://github.com/Pigeon-Home/homing-pigeon/actions/runs/41387454749 , still in progress at the time of this note. Counts from that `/bin/sh` are not in hand. No substitute shell was used.

4. `script_url` encoding. Branch `script-url-encoding`, commit `da2f810d`, pushed 2026-11-02 04:27 UTC. A BOM-less UTF-8 `.ps1` fetched as bytes gains one UTF-8 mark after the hash, and its newline stays a newline. A file that already has the mark, a file that is not UTF-8, and a script that is not a `.ps1` are left as they arrived. The tests are `runner/tests/test_script_url_encoding.py`, four of them, all passing here.

